11.1 Gate Criteria

Progression from Phase 1 to Phase 2 requires:

\begin{cases}
H_1 \text{ supported with } d \geq 0.5 \\
\text{Measurement validated with } r \geq 0.4 \\
\text{No manipulation effect} \\
\text{No safety incidents}
\end{cases}

If these criteria are not met, the project does not proceed. It either revises and repeats AWA-0, or concludes that adaptation does not enhance wonder under these conditions.

Both outcomes are informative. The project is not a success only if the criteria are met; it is a success if it produces knowledge—including knowledge that the original hypothesis was wrong.

